\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 General Notes\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\sa120 Generic IP driver for any projector that supports PJLink Class 1 (Epson, Sony, NEC/Sharp, Panasonic, Optoma, Hitachi/Maxell, Canon, Christie, BenQ and others). Control is over TCP port 4352.\par
\pard\ql\sa120 Fully tested on Control4 with a Panasonic PT-VMZ51S. It should work with any PJLink projector: run the List Projector Inputs action to see which inputs the projector has, then change the input codes directly in the driver properties.\par
\pard\ql\sa120\i AI code generation was used in the production and testing of this driver. No warranty is provided. Please report bugs at github.com/jwheeler188/PJFree/issues so the driver can be improved. Released into the public domain under The Unlicense.\i0\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Setup\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 1.\tab Enable PJLink in the projector's network menu. Note the PJLink password if authentication is on.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 2.\tab Set the projector's standby mode so the network stays active while it is off. Eco or low-power standby usually disables the LAN, and power-on will not work.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 3.\tab Enter the projector's IP Address in the driver properties.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 4.\tab Enter the Password if PJLink authentication is on. Leave it blank if it is off.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 5.\tab In Connections > Control/AV, bind your sources to the projector inputs and set the projector as the room's video end-point.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 6.\tab Run the Query Status action. Projector Name, Power State and Lamp Hours should populate.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Inputs\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\sa120 Each input has a PJLink Code property that sets the INPT code sent for it. Defaults match the Panasonic PT-VMZ51S:\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b HDMI 1\b0  - 31\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b HDMI 2\b0  - 32\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Computer 1\b0  - 11\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Computer 2\b0  - 12\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Memory Viewer\b0  - 41\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Network / USB\b0  - 51\par
\pard\ql\sa120 PJLink input ranges: 1x = RGB, 2x = Video, 3x = Digital (HDMI/DVI/HDBaseT), 4x = Storage, 5x = Network. For other projectors, run List Projector Inputs and edit the codes. No driver change is needed.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Driver Properties\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b IP Address\b0  - Projector IP address.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Password\b0  - PJLink password. Leave blank if authentication is off.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Send Auth With Every Command\b0  - Leave at No (per spec). Set Yes only if the projector rejects the second command in a session with an authentication error.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Poll Interval (seconds)\b0  - Default 30. Set 0 to disable polling. Lamp and error status are polled every 10th cycle.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Debug Mode\b0  - Prints PJLink TX/RX traffic to the Lua output window.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Connection Status, Projector Name, Power State, Current Input, Lamp Hours, Error Status\b0  - Read-only status.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b [Input] PJLink Code\b0  - INPT code sent for each Control4 input.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Driver Actions\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Query Status\b0  - Reads name, power, input, AV mute, error status and lamp hours.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Power On / Power Off\b0  - Discrete power.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b List Projector Inputs\b0  - Prints the projector's supported input codes to the Lua output.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Driver Programming\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa40\b\fs22 Commands\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab Power On\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab Power Off\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab AV Mute On\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab AV Mute Off\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab Send PJLink Command - for example AVMT 31 or INPT 32. Leave out the %1 prefix.\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa40\b\fs22 Variables\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b POWER_STATE\b0  - Off / On / Cooling / Warming Up\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b POWER_ON\b0  - 0 / 1 (warming up counts as on)\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b INPUT\b0  - Current input name\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b AV_MUTE\b0  - 0 / 1\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b LAMP_HOURS\b0  - Hours per lamp\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b ERROR_STATUS\b0  - OK, or a list such as Filter Warning\par
\pard\ql\sb120\sa40\b\fs22 Behavior\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab Selecting a source while the projector is off powers it on. The input command is retried every 5 seconds (up to about 2 minutes) while the projector reports busy during warm-up.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab Warming up counts as ON and cooling down counts as OFF for the room.\par
\pard\ql\fi-240\li480\sa40 \bullet\tab The driver connects on demand and drops the socket when idle, which avoids the projector's 30-second idle timeout.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Testing from the Lua Tab\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\sa120 The Lua Command box runs Lua, not raw PJLink, so wrap commands in Send():\par
\pard\ql\li480\sa20\f1 Send("INPT 32")   -- switch to HDMI 2\f0\par
\pard\ql\li480\sa20\f1 Send("POWR ?")    -- query power\f0\par
\pard\ql\li480\sa20\f1 Send("INST ?")    -- list supported input codes\f0\par
\pard\ql\li480\sa20\f1 QueryAll()        -- full status refresh\f0\par
\pard\ql\sa120 Turn on Debug Mode to see the exchange in the Lua output.\par
\pard\ql\sb240\sa80\b\fs28 Troubleshooting\b0\fs20\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b No response from projector\b0  - Wrong IP, port 4352 blocked, PJLink disabled, or network standby off.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Authentication error (check password)\b0  - PJLink password does not match the projector.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b ERR2 on an input change\b0  - The projector does not use that code. Run List Projector Inputs and fix the code.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b ERR3\b0  - Projector is busy (warming, cooling or off). Input and mute commands retry automatically.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b Will not power on from off\b0  - Network standby is disabled on the projector.\par
\pard\ql\li240\sa40\b '=' expected near ... in the Lua output\b0  - A raw PJLink command was typed in the Lua box. Use Send("...").\par
